# release_notes_updater

Update `RELEASE_NOTES.md` in the project root with player-facing changes — new features, UI improvements, fixes, or technical improvements the player will notice.

The full procedure (format, categorization rules, version bump rules, examples of good vs. bad entries) is in [.claude/skills/release_notes_updater/SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/release_notes_updater/SKILL.md).

Read that file when this rule triggers, then follow it.

**Quick rules:**

- Russian only (target audience: player)
- Categories in order: Новые функции → Улучшения UI → Исправления → Технические улучшения
- New version on top, old versions stay below untouched
- Phrasing from the player's perspective, not the code's
- No class names, file paths, or commit hashes
- No dates (version + position is enough)
- Do NOT use this rule for internal refactoring, dependency bumps, or doc-only changes
